!! Welcome to ~DevThing

"""
`DevThing` is an open source project manager for software development.
It runs 100% on the browser, consisting of a ''single HTML file''.

You can find the source code at https://github.com/ruivieira/devthing.

`DevThing` development is done in `DevThing` itself.
The documentation ''is'' the demo.
"""

!! Projects

To list all the projects, you can use the `<<projects>>` macro. In this case, this will show:

<<projects>>

!!! Sub-projects

"""
Each project may have subprojects.
To create a new subproject, create a new tiddle, tag it as `subproject` and specify the linked project by setting `project` field.
To list all the subprojects, use the macro
"""

```
<<project-subprojects $PROJECT>>
```

For the main [[DevThing core]] project, this would produce

<<project-subprojects "DevThing core">>

"""
To list the issues in a subproject, use the `<<subproject-issues $SUBPROJECT $STATUS>>` macro.
For instance, to list all the closed issues in [[SubProjectUI]] use
`<<subproject-issues "SubProjectUI" "closed">>`. This will produce
"""

<<subproject-issues "SubProjectUI" "closed">>

See below (or [[Issues]]) for details on how to link an issue to a subproject.

More information in [[Projects]].

!! Issues

Any Tiddler tagged with `issue` will be considered an issue. For in depth view of issue fields used by `DevThing` check out
[[Issues]]. It is also possible to create an issue directly from a project just by pressing the
<$button>New issue {{$:/plugins/ruivieira/devthing/images/bug}}</$button> button.
For an example, go to the [[DevThing core]] project.

!!! Status

Issues can have one of the following status. //Open// status can be:

* <<HB 5>> `todo`
* <<HB 8>> `next`
* <<HB 13>> `inprogress`
* {{$:/plugins/ruivieira/devthing/images/onhold}} `onhold`
* <<HB 21>> `review`

A special status is <<HB 34>> `done`. This status allows to filter some lists
in order to remove completed issues.

To show a list of all the issues linked to a specific `$PROJECT`, simply use the macro `<<project-issues $PROJECT $STATUS>>`
with `$STATUS` being either one of the above or, alternatively, `"open"` or `"closed"`. For instance,

```
<<project-issues "DevThing core" "open">>
```

will show all the open ("non-closed") issue for the `DevThing core` project:

<<project-issues "DevThing core" "open">>

A macro to show all the issues for all the projects (group by project) is available as
`<<projects-issues-all $STATUS>>`. An example can be found in the //Projects// tab on
the sidebar or by [[opening that view directly|$:/plugins/ruivieira/devthing/ui/SideBar/ProjectsSideBar]].

!!! Parent issues

[[Issues]] can have sub-issues and parents.
To define it as a sub-issue, define the `issue.parent` field.
As an example you can see [[ISSUE-2]], which is the parent of [[ISSUE-1]].
There is no limit to the nesting level and issues from different projects can be linked.

!!! Sprints

Issues can be linked to a specific Sprint (more information on Sprints below).
To do so, simply fill the `issue.sprint` field.

More information in [[Issues]].

!!! Timeline

To embed an issue timeline the macro

```
<<project-issues-timeline $PROJECT>>
```

can be used. In this particular case this would show all the issues (with due dates) for the [[DevThing core]]
project. Issues on the timeline are clickable.

<<project-issues-timeline "DevThing core">>

!! Line-up

You can add [[Issues]] to a line-up simply by tagging them with `line-up`.
The current line-up can then be checked in two ways.

Either by embedding the line-up anywhere by using the `line-up` macro:

```
<<line-up>>
```

which will, in this instance, show:

<<line-up>>

Or by looking at the //Line-up// tab in the side bar (next to //Open//)

!! Sprints

!!! Current sprint

Sprint workflow is not necessary in order to use `DevThing`, but it is supported.

Sprints can be defined by adding the `sprint` tag.
Some mandatory fields are `sprint.start` and `sprint.end`. The date format is currently `YYYY-MM-DD`.

To get the current sprint name use the macro

```
<<current-sprint $PROJECT>>
```

which will generarate, in this instance:

<<current-sprint "DevThing core">>

!!! All sprints

To list all sprints, use the macro

```
<<project-sprints $PROJECT>>
```

which in this case will produce

<<project-sprints "DevThing core">>

The current sprint will be labelled with {{$:/plugins/ruivieira/devthing/images/sprint-black}},
all other ones are labelled with {{$:/plugins/ruivieira/devthing/images/sprint-faded}}.

!!! Sprint issues

To list issues from a specific project and sprint, you can use the macro

```
<<project-sprint-issues $PROJECT $SPRINT $STATUS>>
```

Even though `$SPRINT` has an unique name, you should specify the `$PROJECT`, since issues from
more than one project might happen in the same sprint, if that is your workflow.

As an example, calling `<<project-sprint-issues "DevThing core" "Sprint2" "all">>` shows

<<project-sprint-issues "DevThing core" "Sprint2" "all">>

!!! Timeline

To embed an issue timeline the macro

```
<<project-sprints-timeline $PROJECT>>
```

can be used. In this particular case this would show all the sprints for the [[DevThing core]]
project. Sprints on the timeline are clickable.

<<project-sprints-timeline "DevThing core">>

!! Tasks

Tasks are lightweight units of work.
Tasks are linked to a project and are created by tagging a tiddler with `task` and setting a `task.project`.
Optionally a `task.date.due` date can be added. By default, tasks have a `task.status: open`.
It is also possible to create a task directly from a project just by pressing the 
<$button>New task {{$:/core/images/done-button}}</$button> button.
For an example, go to the [[DevThing core]] project.


The macro `<<tasks $PROJECT $STATUS>>` lists the links to all `$PROJECT` tasks with status `$STATUS`.
For instance, `<<tasks "DevThing core" "all">>` shows all tasks (open and closed) for this project:

<<tasks "DevThing core" "all">>

Tasks can be directly opened or closed from their listings (try it above).

Tasks due //today// have the {{$:/plugins/ruivieira/devthing/images/due-today}} flag, while //overdue// tasks
have the {{$:/plugins/ruivieira/devthing/images/due-overdue}} flag.

!! Agenda

You can embed an agenda for all issues and tasks with the macro `<<agenda>>`. This would produce the result below:

<<agenda>>

You can also see the [[$:/plugins/ruivieira/devthing/ui/SideBar/AgendaSideBar]] sidebar in the right, next to the
//Projects// sidebar.

!! Other features

!!! Syntax highlighting

Syntax highlighting supported within code blocks.

```java
// Parallel Processing
import java.util.List;

List<String> dataList = null;
dataList.parallelStream().map(line -> processItem(line));
```

!!! Diagram support

Diagrams are supported using the `mermaid.js` plugin.
The diagram code can be embeded using the `<$mermaid text=$DIAGRAM></$mermaid>` macro.
For instance

```
<$mermaid text="
graph LR
  A[Project] -->|optional| B(Sprint)
  B -->D[ISSUE-1]
  B -->E[ISSUE-2]
  A -->F[ISSUE-3]
"></$mermaid>
```

produces

<$mermaid text="
graph LR
  A[Project] -->|optional| B(Sprint)
  B -->D[ISSUE-1]
  B -->E[ISSUE-2]
  A -->F[ISSUE-3]
"></$mermaid>

!!! Vim key bindings

`DevThing` supports Vim key bindings when editing tiddlers.

However, due to `ESC` closing the editor, it is recommended to use `Ctrl+C` to change Vim modes.

The keymap can be changed at [[$:/config/codemirror/keyMap]].